Preamble

The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for
software and other kinds of works.

The licenses for most software are designed to take away your freedom to
share and change. By contrast, the GNU AGPL is designed to guarantee
your freedom to share and change all versions of a program.

When you share a program with other users, the GNU AGPL ensures that
everyone receives the same rights that you received. It also makes it
impossible to make a proprietary version of the program and sell it
without making the source code available to everyone else.

It is your freedom to:
- Share copies of the software with others
- Study the source code and change it
- Distribute modified versions to others

However, you must:
- Release the source code under this license
- Provide source code with binary distributions
- Make the source available to users who receive the program
- Release modifications under the same license (AGPL-3.0)

